-- title:
--   The Clifford gate set (single-qubit gates in $\langle H, S\rangle$ and CNOT)
-- statement:
--   The gates a Clifford circuit is built from. The paper defines the $n$-qubit Clifford group as
--   $$
--   \mathrm{Cl}(n) := \langle H_j, S_j, \mathrm{CNOT}_{j,k} : j, k\in[n],\ j\neq k\rangle \le \mathrm{SU}(2^n) \qquad (2.55).
--   $$
--   Accordingly, the Clifford gate set consists of
--
--   1. every single-qubit gate whose $2\times2$ matrix lies in the subgroup $\langle H, S\rangle$ of $\mathrm U(2)$ generated by the Hadamard and phase gates, and
--   2. the two-qubit CNOT gate.
--
--   The finite group $\langle H, S\rangle$ contains $I$, $Z = S^2$, $S^\dagger = S^3$, $X = HS^2H$ and the scalars $e^{ik\pi/4}$, since $(HS)^3 = e^{i\pi/4}I$ (p.16). Placing CNOT with either qubit as control gives both orientations. A depth-1 Clifford circuit is a single layer of such gates on pairwise disjoint qubits.
--
--   **Formalization Note** The CNOT gate is the base mission's published `DepthOneQExp.cnotGate` (wire 0 is the control). No other two-qubit gate (CZ, SWAP) is included, and neither is any single-qubit gate outside $\langle H, S\rangle$.
-- source:
--   Anshu–Balasubramanian–Haferkamp–Harrow–Tan, Depth-1 expanders on the unitary group and applications, arXiv:2609.01605 (held version, sha256 3c3f8513…aebfd87), §2.4, Eq. (2.55), p.15

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_MITMSynthesis_Gate
import Definitions.Def_DepthOneQExp_cnotGate
import Definitions.Def_DepthOneQExp_Supplement_hGate
import Definitions.Def_DepthOneQExp_Supplement_sGate

namespace DepthOneQExp.Supplement

/-- **The Clifford gate set** (Anshu–Balasubramanian–Haferkamp–Harrow–Tan, *Depth-1 expanders on the unitary group and
applications*, arXiv:2609.01605, held version sha256 3c3f8513…aebfd87, §2.4, Eq. (2.55), p.15: the Clifford circuit group is
`Cl(n) := ⟨H_j, S_j, CNOT_{j,k}⟩ ⩽ SU(2ⁿ)`): the single-qubit gates whose matrix lies in the
subgroup `⟨H, S⟩` of `U(2)` generated by the Hadamard and phase gates, together with the CNOT gate.

**Formalization Note** `⟨H, S⟩` is a finite group; it contains `I`, `Z = S²`, `S† = S³`,
`X = H S² H` and the scalars `e^{ikπ/4}` (`(HS)³ = e^{iπ/4} I`, p.16). A gate of a Clifford circuit
is either one such single-qubit gate or a CNOT (`DepthOneQExp.cnotGate`, wire `0` the control);
placing `cnotGate` on qubits `(a, b)` or `(b, a)` gives both orientations. No other two-qubit
gates (`CZ`, `SWAP`) and no single-qubit gate outside `⟨H, S⟩` are allowed. -/
def cliffordGateSet : Set MITMSynthesis.Gate :=
  {g | ∃ U ∈ Subgroup.closure
      ({hGate.mat, sGate.mat} : Set (Matrix.unitaryGroup (MITMSynthesis.Q 1) ℂ)),
      g = ⟨1, one_pos, U⟩} ∪ {cnotGate}

end DepthOneQExp.Supplement


